{"mines":[{"county":"Esmeralda","district":"Goldfield","evidence":[{"basis":"1913-1915 shipped ore","evidence_id":"nv-grizzly-bear-1913-15","measurements":[{"commodity":"Au","unit":"troy_ounces_per_short_ton","value":1.07},{"commodity":"Ag","unit":"troy_ounces_per_short_ton","value":5.58},{"commodity":"Cu","unit":"percent","value":4.21}],"page_cite":"p. 17","page_text_sha256":"fce3cda1e63739346e1d0e8f371e78e5e06f6a2eb9f8f54b28313eb69afa70ba","quote_verbatim":true,"source_id":"nbmg-mdf-21600019","verbatim_quote":"The production of such ore from the Grizzly Bear shaft in 1913-15, inclusive, was 22,408 short dry tons, assaying 1.07 oz. Au., 5.58 oz. Ag. and 4.21% Cu.","years":"1913-1915"}],"mine_id":"nv-grizzly-bear-shaft","name":"Grizzly Bear shaft"},{"county":"Esmeralda","district":"Goldfield","evidence":[{"basis":"1915 shipped ore","evidence_id":"nv-jumbo-extension-1915","measurements":[{"commodity":"Au","unit":"troy_ounces_per_short_ton","value":1.35},{"commodity":"Ag","unit":"troy_ounces_per_short_ton","value":4.41},{"commodity":"Cu","unit":"percent","value":2.79}],"page_cite":"p. 18","page_text_sha256":"8cbefedcd909a6d41b72165e98bad728bb6555e9e116d369c730ee9396fe2d59","quote_verbatim":true,"source_id":"nbmg-mdf-21600019","verbatim_quote":"The Jumbo Extension during the year 1915 shipped 22,562 tons, averaging 1.35 oz. Au., 4.41 oz. Ag., and 2.79% Cu.","years":"1915"}],"mine_id":"nv-jumbo-extension","name":"Jumbo Extension"},{"county":"Esmeralda","district":"Goldfield","evidence":[{"basis":"reported crosscut samples","evidence_id":"nv-florence-west-crosscut-samples","measurements":[{"commodity":"Au","unit":"troy_ounces_per_short_ton","value":5}],"page_cite":"p. 24","page_text_sha256":"04f4088d9cb3f557612556f5432be9a135b0ff6177f46d4f7a744a6181d01257","quote_verbatim":true,"source_id":"nbmg-mdf-21600019","verbatim_quote":"The most important of these veins, as at present developed, may be actually seen departing from the low-grade pyritic mineralization of the Columbia Mountain fault, like a branch from a tree trunk; samples containing five ounces gold can be cut across the branch vein within six feet of the apparently earlier flat-dipping pyritic quartz which carries only five dollars per ton.","years":"1947 report"}],"mine_id":"nv-florence-west-crosscut","name":"Florence mine western crosscut branch vein"},{"county":"Nye","district":"Bullfrog","evidence":[{"basis":"bonanza ore above the 200-foot level","evidence_id":"nv-montgomery-shoshone-bonanza","measurements":[{"commodity":"Ag","unit":"troy_ounces_per_short_ton","value":600}],"page_cite":"p. 91","page_text_sha256":"cdc776a4df95d83072d727ca94b1b7e3a5283b1982acc2607ea0efbff0f2ecb1","quote_verbatim":true,"source_id":"usgs-b407","verbatim_quote":"Even in the Bonanza ore of the Montgomery-Shoshone mine above the 200-foot level, much of which averaged over 600 ounces of silver to the ton","years":"1905-1908"}],"mine_id":"nv-montgomery-shoshone","name":"Montgomery-Shoshone mine"},{"county":"Elko","district":"Cornucopia","evidence":[{"basis":"reported mill runs","evidence_id":"nv-leopard-mill-runs","measurements":[{"commodity":"Ag","unit":"troy_ounces_per_short_ton","value":400}],"page_cite":"p. 64","page_text_sha256":"8c929561e078474f2a9e27af7871d2978763bbac116d0d12bebc2f87df2a5056","quote_verbatim":true,"source_id":"usgs-b408","verbatim_quote":"The proportion of the sulphides present is very small; but they must have been rich, for the ore is said to have carried 400 ounces of silver to the ton for mill runs.","years":"by 1908"}],"mine_id":"nv-leopard-mine","name":"Leopard mine"},{"county":"Elko","district":"Edgemont","evidence":[{"basis":"mill feed","evidence_id":"nv-lucky-girl-mill-feed","measurements":[{"commodity":"Ag","unit":"troy_ounces_per_short_ton","value":1}],"page_cite":"pp. 75-76","page_text_sha256":"f2149713492032b419effeb06270b65b59449bc7b6a88a802bc2ba18bd614080","quote_verbatim":true,"source_id":"usgs-b408","verbatim_quote":"The total extraction is from 90 to 95 